t with a car is because last time I  checked cars didn't give you any rent  cars don't give you any money so in that  five years how are you going to get the  money to pay for the car if you can't  afford it now how you're gonna be able  to afford it in five years time so the  whole idea of buying something now I'm  paying for it later generally is  probably not that smart you buy a  holiday now you go to pay for it later  the holidays finished and you've still  got the debt however we  a property a lease option agreement  number one you don't have to buy the  property at the end of the five years so  you can with a lease option agreement at  the end of the five years you can walk  away and hand the keys back and pay  nothing now that's why it's called lease  option and not lease obligation however  the seller has to let you exercise your  option so it's kind of like a having  your cake and eat it so that's the first  great thing about doing lease option  agreements within residential property  imagine if you drove a car around for  five years and you hadn't paid a penny  then you went now change my mind and  you're handed it back that'll be amazing  well that's what you can do with  properties however on top of that  properties tend to go up in value not  down so if you agree to buy a property  now for a hundred thousand pounds and  then in five years time or seven years  time however long you agree this period  over in seven years time what happens if  the house is worth 150 or 200 thousand  pounds and this is something that's  happened to me many many times well what  happens is suddenly you've got yourself  an absolute bargain of a property deal  and you've had five years or seven years  to save up for that properties that's  the second amazing thing about lease  option agreements and the third amazing  thing about these option agreements are  if you are buying the property now but  paying for it later  you get the keys now but you've not paid  anything what are you going to do with  that property you're going to rent it  out so you're going to start benefiting  from monthly cash flow now you might be  thinking now Samuel sounds good in fact  Samuel it almost sounds a little bit too  good and if something sounds too good to  be true it usually is listen in most of  my videos when I talk about property  investment strategies I talk about the  good I talk about the bad and there's  often a lot of bad with lease option  agreements honestly there's very little  bad the only bad thing is is actually  finding a seller that's up willing to  pass your prop let you have it on a  lease option agreement you don't come  across those types of sellers every hour  or every day you've got to work to find  those sellers so and also of lease  option agreements just because you don't  pay anything now  going to put this out as a disclaimer  you do have to pay the legal fees so  you're gonna have to pay a solicitor to  draw up the contracts which will cost  maybe around a thousand pounds also you  will need to pay a one pound option fee  in order to make the contracts legal so  there's gonna be a little bit of money  but with that you have a property and  you rent it out and you get the cash  flow from the rent and you're  benefitting from the capital  appreciation so if the only negative is  finding the sellers the question is are  there any sellers that would do this and  you might be again thinking like  thinking right now no one would do that  no one would pass their house on to me  on a lease option agreement where I  could buy it now and pay for it later  who would do that in their right mind  let me tell you exactly who will do this  because there are people doing it I've  secured many Lease Option agreements my  students have secured many Lease Option  agreements and the reason the way you to  do it is you need to find sellers who  either don't need or can't get the money  now so if someone's selling their house  because they need them money now you buy  it they use that money to buy another  house to live in that's not going to  work for a lease option agreement but if  you find people are selling their houses  who've inherited their house and they're  like oh I've got this house I don't know  what to do with it I don't live near it  what you know they don't need the money  if they sell it they're just gonna use  the money to put in the back and just  have it in savings for those types of  people that are struggling to sell a  lease option agreement can be perfect  because you're taking the property off  of their hands you're green to buy it  down the line and what you normally do  the lease option agreement is you pay a  small monthly fee second type of people  are people in negative equity so if  you've got a property where your  mortgage is really high and the value of  your house is lower than the mortgage  outstanding and by the way that's  happening more than ever right now in  2020 because of Corona and the epidemic  and what's going on property prices are  dipping which is leaving people with a  higher mortgage than the value of their  house so those types of people that want  to sell they can't sell and even if they  did sell and someone paid them the the  asking price all they do with that money  is they'd use it to pay off the mortgage  those are the types of  people where their house to them that  even want it they've got no equity in it  where you can secure a buy now pay later  lease option agreement and when you can  find those people you can then begin to  build your portfolio using very very  very little money now if you want to  learn more about this strategy of lease  option agreements I do sometimes run  free webinars where I give advanced  training on this strategy and go through  exactly how to find these types of  sellers in the description on this video  you can click the link and you can leave  your details and I will let you know  you'll be the first to know when I'm  